# Projection: GMEOW → pure odrl. GENERATED by `gmeow-dev sync --mode update --outputs generated` (mappings) from canonical mapping sources — DO NOT EDIT.
# Lossy and directional by design; drops: GMEOW extension RightsAction values with no exact ODRL action IRI are passed through under odrl:action; the rule remains machine-readable without fabricating a target vocabulary term; ODRL logical-constraint boolean operators (and/or/xone) are not emitted; atomic-constraint shells and right operands project here, while left operands and comparison operators are rewritten by the exact value-table cells below; the licence's gmeow:licenseFamily / validFrom / validUntil / spdxLicenseId are dropped; only the ODRL offer skeleton survives; the permission's own odrl:constraint (e.g. temporal validity) does not propagate to the duty — ODRL 2.2 does not inherit a permission's constraints onto its duties, so the duty's constraint scope must be stated separately on the duty rule; the conformance claim is carried exactly as declared by the policy author — the transpiler never verifies it; odrl:uid is the policy node's own IRI; no independent GMEOW uid predicate exists to recover from the target property alone.
